@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# Arise Store shop assistant
+
+`POST /api/v1/marketplace/assistant` is a read-only bridge endpoint. It reuses the
+configured AI Gateway primary/fallback configuration, with a 12-second request
+budget. No API key, model or seller billing configuration is added or changed.
+
+The `marketplace-chat-v2` model contract returns conversation/search intent, evidence IDs and keyword
+synonyms, never unchecked customer-facing prose, product facts, payment instructions or
+orders. Application code returns a `reply` paragraph instead of exposing knowledge
+labels or raw settings to the customer. Greetings, product suggestions, clarifications
+and failures use conversational text; customer language and merchant dialect reuse
+the Inbox language helpers. COD replies reuse the Inbox policy renderer and the
+actual marketplace payment eligibility, including selected-product overrides. False
+and missing settings stay distinct; eligible areas, delivery charges and any advance
+remain checkout-owned. No boolean or internal COD enum is presented as a reply. Budget, size and color spans must occur in customer text. Code applies
+Decimal budgets and current variant stock/size/color to the published catalog.
+Each returned card includes the fresh source product; browser catalog snapshots
+do not supply the displayed price or stock. Checkout still revalidates everything.
+
+The launcher exists only inside shop routes. A shop change unmounts the drawer and clears its in-memory conversation. Both bridge layers require an available published shop. The storefront overwrites client-supplied knowledge and product allowlists with its own shop pages and moderated catalog.
+The source intersects it with current published products and mandatory shop scope.
+Customer searches are bounded to 1,000 characters plus four previous user queries.
+The model receives search text and bounded, tenant-scoped evidence: shop profile, canonical policies, current indexed knowledge, and Arise Store pages loaded by the trusted bridge. Internal, inactive, stale and conflicting knowledge is excluded. It selects evidence IDs; application code composes readable paragraphs from eligible saved passages, never unchecked generated policy claims. The legacy `information` payload is no longer returned. Customer orders and other shops are excluded.
+There are no conversation/customer-message writes, cart mutations or order actions. Before inference, consume_merchant_ai_quota(commit=False) reserves one message under the existing canonical-owner/store/credit transaction locks, never the visitor's quota. Successful replies commit that unit; unavailable results, exceptions and cancellation roll it back. Failed reservations never dispatch provider work. No new billing ledger or migration is needed. The lock spans the gateway's bounded inference, so concurrent quota consumers for the same owner wait; unrelated owners use different locks. Provider failures remain uncharged to the merchant, even when a failed provider attempt costs the operator.
+The source Redis gate and storefront metadata gate each allow 30 searches per
+customer per hour; storefront also admits at most 120 per IP per hour. Admission
+storage failures fail closed. Existing gateway key accounting remains active.
+
+Stock-zero variants and non-BDT prices under a BDT budget are excluded. Unsupported
+amounts, ambiguous requests and malformed responses ask for clarification. Missing
+provider configuration, timeouts and provider failures show an unavailable state;
+they never claim inventory is empty. Gift requests without a category ask which
+kind of product the buyer wants. No popularity, comfort, delivery-date or conversion
+claims are generated. Policy/tracking requests link to existing scoped information
+or authenticated tracking rather than reveal private order information.
+
+Voice input uses the browser's SpeechRecognition service when available. Customers
+review/edit the Bangla transcript before submitting. No audio upload endpoint or
+audio/transcript persistence is added. Browser support and microphone permission
+are required; typing remains available.
+
+Offline tests use mocked providers and do not spend merchant/provider credit or
+send messages. Live provider relevance, real Bengali microphone recognition,
+production load and a merchant pilot are not verified. Before rollout, configure
+and review the existing gateway, test isolated real-model queries, then review a
+limited store pilot; do not claim the social sales-AI release gate has passed.
+
+Rollback removes the Store launcher and assistant bridge routes. No commerce data,
+metadata migration or environment variable is introduced. Existing crafts and
+ordinary checkout do not depend on the assistant.
+
+The Store endpoint respects customer_ai_paused (manual snake/camel settings and configured AI business hours) before quota admission or provider calls. Paused shops return unavailable without charging. The UI uses a shop-branded violet chat header, user/assistant bubbles, starter prompts, a compact send-arrow composer and typing state. Enter sends, Shift+Enter inserts a line, and IME composition does not submit. Voice is transcript-first. Legacy backend information cards are ignored by the UI. AI identity and a real contact-seller link remain explicit; no human handoff or order action is claimed.
