@@ -7,6 +7,27 @@ migration, storage provisioning, live Meta delivery and browser visual review ha

 ## Merchant and customer behavior

+- `store_upload` tracks newly written objects in the current AsyncSession root or
+  savepoint transaction. A successful commit retains them; savepoint release promotes
+  pending cleanup to its parent. Rollback and session close await physical deletion,
+  including failures after a successful upload returned. This also covers craft
+  checkout media preservation. Deduplicated committed objects are never registered.
+  Threaded writes/deletes finish before cancellation propagates, preventing a late
+  writer from recreating a deleted object. Existing quota and validation limits stay
+  in place. Native craft tests exercise real request rollback, local files and fake
+  S3 for late validation, response-construction and pre-persistence commit failures.
+  This is best-effort compensation, not distributed atomicity: process termination,
