+# Marketplace recovery unavailable
+
+The Source phone recovery endpoints fail closed with 503 because the repository has
+no verified phone OTP delivery service. Challenge disclosure, the fixed substitute,
+in-memory fallback and the recovery rebinding path have been removed. Existing
+Redis challenges cannot authorize requests; no new challenge or phone-based order
+count is returned. Normal browser/account-owned purchases and tracking remain.
+The Store removes its unsupported email-code form and links to My purchases; no
+public recovery proxy or new delivery dependency was added. Future recovery needs
+real delivery, caller/account-bound one-use proof, bounded attempts and the normal
+marketplace/account eligibility checks before any order projection or mutation.
+
+# Transactional image cleanup
+
+Uncommitted image files follow their owning database transaction across API and
+worker sessions. Rollback or close awaits cleanup of new files; a released savepoint
+keeps its files pending until the outer transaction commits. Committed and reused
+assets are retained. No new table or cleanup service was added. Crashes, uncertain
+commit outcomes and storage deletion failures still require operator reconciliation;
+delete failures log the storage/key without exposing provider exception content.
+
+# Catalog policy import permissions
+
+Saving or retiring website policies during catalog import requires the selected
+shop's Brain-write authority, including imports with no new products. The shared
+resolver enforces canonical ownership, current member permissions and view-only
+restrictions under the store lock. Imports that opt out of policy saving keep
+their existing catalog flow; no schema or additional permission model was added.
+
+# Product image ownership
+
+Product image capability issuance now checks product/gallery/asset tenant binding.
+Catalog create/update/import reject asset-reference URLs supplied as external images;
+legacy URL-only records cannot renew a signed asset capability. Normal external
+images and validated own-shop uploads keep their existing flows. Existing bearer
+links are not revoked by this code change and retain their original expiry.
+
+# Marketplace finder quota admission
+
+The Store shopping finder reserves one canonical-owner message in the existing
+quota transaction before provider inference. Successful replies commit; unavailable
+results, exceptions and cancellation roll back the reservation. The owner/store
+locks serialize same-owner quota consumers during the bounded gateway call. No
+schema or billing ledger was added. PostgreSQL race regressions live in
+`backend/tests/test_marketplace_assistant.py`; local/production validation status
+must be reported separately from the implementation.
+
+
+# Conversational Store assistant
+
+The shop assistant now returns customer-facing paragraphs through `marketplace-chat-v2`,
+using the Inbox language and policy helpers. COD uses actual marketplace/selected-product
+payment eligibility, not raw `cod_enabled` or `cod_policy` values. The browser shows
+chat bubbles, Send/Enter input and a real seller-contact link. Model prose never
+becomes transaction evidence; existing owner quota, pause and shop-scope gates remain.
+No human agent message, conversation database, or checkout action was added.
